&P142047 = VS 10, 193 
#atf: lang sux 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. enuru{+e2-nu-ru} 
#tr.en: enuru: 
2. lu2-ra musz mu-ra gir2 mu-ra ur mu2-da mu-ra 
#tr.en: A man a snake struck, a scorpion struck, a rabid dog struck, 
3. usz-bi mu-na-ab-szum2 
#tr.en: their spittle gave. 
# erasure after szum2 
4. {d}asar:lu2-hi-e 
#tr.en: Asarluḫi 
5. a-ni {d}en-ki-sze3 lu2 mu-szi-gi4-gi4 
#tr.en: to his father Enki a messenger sends: 
6. a-mu lu2-ra musz mu-ra gir2 mu-ra ur mu2-da mu-ra 
#tr.en: “My father, a man a snake struck, a scorpion struck, a rabid dog struck,
7. usz-bi mu-na-ab-szum2 
#tr.en: their spittle gave; 
8. a-na ib2-ak-na-bi nu-zu 
#tr.en: what to do about it, I don't know.” 
9. dumu-mu a-na nu-zu 
#tr.en: “My son, what don't you know? 
10. a-na na-ab-dah-e 
#tr.en: What can I add? 
@reverse 
1. a-la2-ku3-ga na-ba-ni-zalag 
#tr.en: His silver ala is purified; 
2. a-be2 nam-szub u3-ma-szum2 
#tr.en: once to the water the incantation is given, 
3. a-bi lu2 kur2-ra u3-mu-ni-nag 
#tr.en: the water the ‘foreigner’ made to drink, 
4. usz-bi ni2-ba ha-mu-ta-e3-de2 
#tr.en: may the spittle on its own go out!” 
$ blank space 
5. lu2 musz zu2 ba-du3 a-bi lu2 kur2-ra na8-na8-da-kam 
#tr.en: A man by a snake bitten: the water the ‘foreigner’ is to be given to drink.

