&P345433 = TCL 16, 89
#atf: lang sux 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. igi musz-husz igi lu2-[ulu3] musz-husz 
#tr.en: The dragon-face (is) the dragon-face of a man, 
2. igi lu2 nig2-hul-dim2#-ma musz-husz 
#tr.en: the dragon-face of a man causing evil 
3. an-ne2 ba-te im szeg3-szeg3 
#tr.en: approached heaven (and) the clouds bring (no) rain. 
4. ki-a ba-te {u2}szim nu-mu2-mu2 
#tr.en: He approached the earth, and the plants do not grow. 
5. gu4-e ba-te {gesz}szudul5-bi im-du8 
#tr.en: He approached the ox, and its yoke does not open.
6. e2-tur3-e ba-te ga-ra-bi im-ta-kum-kum 
#tr.en: He approached the stall and smashes its cheese-pot. 
7. inim gar-ra ha-ba-an-dib-dib
#tr.en: Utterances have passed by.
8. gurusz-ra mu-na-te ib2-la2 mu-da-an-gaz 
#tr.en: He approached the lad and sapped his (sexual) energies, 
9. sikil-ra mu-na-te tug2 mu-da-an-szub 
#tr.en: he approached the maiden and tossed away her towel. 
10. um-me-da dumu-da mu-na-te lirum-bi mu-e-du8 
#tr.en: He approached the nurse with the child - her arms were torn apart.
11. |SAR.SAR|-e ba-te i-iz za3-hi-li im-hul
#tr.en: He approached the vegetables - lettuce and cress became bad.
12. pu2 {gesz}kiri6 ba-te gurun im-hul
#tr.en: He approached the garden, the fruit became bad.
13. igi kur-ra kur-ta nam-ta-an-e3
#tr.en: The eye of the mountain came out from the mountain,
14. szeg9-bar-re si-musz-bi nam-ta-an-e3
#tr.en: The wild ram let its shining horns come out.
15. igi hul igi gig-ga he2-tar
#tr.en: May the evil eye (like?) the sick eye be cut off.
16. {kusz}a-ga2-la2-gin7 he2-dar
#tr.en: May it split open like a leather bag.
17. {dug}sila3-bur-zi bahar2-ka tilla2-a he2-gaz-gaz
#tr.en: May it go to pieces (like) the potter's bur-zi-pot on the market place.
18. gub-bu-da-ba gub-bu-da-ba
#tr.en: While standing, while standing,
19. ka e-sir2-ra-ka gub-bu-da-ba
#tr.en: while standing at the mouth? of the street,
20. szul dingir nu-tuku gaba im-ma-an-ri
#tr.en: it opposes the young man who has no personal god.
@reverse
1. igi lil2-am3 he2-sig3-ge
#tr.en: Let the eye turn into a wind.
2. {d}asar-e abzu-a
#tr.en: Asar in Abzu,
3. nam-mu-un-da-bur2-e
#tr.en: may he not undo it!
$blank

